[38;5;231m⏺[39m Before I touch it — this is removing the only auth check on the route, so I want the consequence on the record first.

  [38;5;153mserver.js:7[39m is the sole caller of [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m. Dropping it makes [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m — which returns actual revenue rows —
  readable by anyone who can reach the process, with no credential at all. Two things make "it's internal" a claim I'd
  want confirmed rather than assumed:

  - [38;5;153mserver.js:11[39m binds [38;5;153mapp.listen[39m with no host argument, so Express listens on all interfaces, not just loopback.
    Whether that's actually unreachable from outside depends on network config I can't see from here.
  - [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m becomes dead code after this, so the next admin route added has no guard sitting next to it as a
    pattern to copy.

  The 401 is also what makes the dashboard script fail loudly today; without it a misrouted or compromised caller gets
  revenue data and a 200.
